<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
	xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
	<modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
	<parent>
		<groupId>nl.utwente.groove</groupId>
		<artifactId>assembly</artifactId>
		<version>1.0</version>
	</parent>
	<artifactId>groove-yfiles-bin</artifactId>
	<packaging>pom</packaging>

	<!-- The yFiles zip, groove-x_y_z-yfiles-bin.zip (only under the yfiles
	     profile): the plain bin zip with the two obfuscated jars of the yfiles
	     module in lib/, launchers whose class path lists them, and the yFiles
	     notice at the root. See zip.xml, and release/README.md. -->

	<properties>
		<output-suffix>yfiles-bin</output-suffix>
		<yfiles.zip>true</yfiles.zip>
		<!-- the run of the Imager on the zip's content (check-yfiles-zip below);
		     skip with -Dyfiles.smoke.skip=true -->
		<yfiles.smoke.skip>false</yfiles.smoke.skip>
		<smoke.grammar>${project.basedir}/../../../junit/samples/circularlist4.gps</smoke.grammar>
	</properties>

	<dependencies>
		<dependency>
			<!-- orders the reactor after the obfuscation. Its own dependencies,
			     the plain backend and library jars among them, are excluded, so
			     that they are in the dependency graph of no assembling module:
			     the include filter of the dependency set is lenient (see
			     ../bin/zip.xml), and a plain library jar in a zip would breach the
			     yFiles licence -->
			<groupId>${project.groupId}</groupId>
			<artifactId>yfiles-obfuscated</artifactId>
			<version>${project.version}</version>
			<type>pom</type>
			<exclusions>
				<exclusion>
					<groupId>*</groupId>
					<artifactId>*</artifactId>
				</exclusion>
			</exclusions>
		</dependency>
	</dependencies>

	<build>
		<plugins>
			<plugin>
				<artifactId>maven-assembly-plugin</artifactId>
			</plugin>
			<plugin>
				<!-- the check of the zip, after the assembly, and the checks of the
				     yFiles zip in particular -->
				<artifactId>maven-antrun-plugin</artifactId>
				<executions>
					<execution>
						<!-- What the yFiles zip must hold beyond the plain bin zip,
						     checked on the zip itself: in lib/, exactly the two jars
						     of the yfiles module besides the jars of the plain zip,
						     each byte for byte the obfuscated one and not its input
						     (the licence check of the yfiles module, which inspects
						     its output, then holds for the zip as well); the
						     restrictions that come with yFiles are at its root, in
						     LICENSE-YFILES.txt; and the
						     launchers of the zip, unpacked, must render a grammar
						     on the yFiles backend. The Imager falls back to JGraph
						     with a warning when the backend is missing, so the
						     check looks for that warning, and a plain launcher run
						     on the same tree must print it, which keeps the check
						     from going blind if the wording of the warning
						     changes. -->
						<id>check-yfiles-zip</id>
						<phase>package</phase>
						<goals>
							<goal>run</goal>
						</goals>
						<configuration>
							<target xmlns:unless="ant:unless">
								<property name="zip" location="${zip.file}" />
								<property name="check.dir" location="${project.build.directory}/yfiles-check" />
								<property name="obf.dir" location="${project.basedir}/../../yfiles/target" />
								<property name="plain.zip" location="${project.basedir}/../../target/groove-${groove-version-underscored}-bin.zip" />
								<delete dir="${check.dir}" />
								<mkdir dir="${check.dir}" />
								<fail message="The plain bin zip ${plain.zip}, against which the lib/ of the yFiles zip is checked, is missing; build the whole release reactor.">
									<condition>
										<not>
											<available file="${plain.zip}" type="file" />
										</not>
									</condition>
								</fail>
								<pathconvert property="lib.plain" pathsep=" ">
									<sort>
										<zipfileset src="${plain.zip}" includes="*/lib/*" />
									</sort>
									<flattenmapper />
								</pathconvert>
								<pathconvert property="lib.rest" pathsep=" ">
									<sort>
										<zipfileset src="${zip}" includes="*/lib/*" excludes="*/lib/${backend.jar} */lib/${yfiles.jar}" />
									</sort>
									<flattenmapper />
								</pathconvert>
								<resourcecount property="lib.yfiles.count">
									<zipfileset src="${zip}" includes="*/lib/${backend.jar} */lib/${yfiles.jar}" />
								</resourcecount>
								<!-- (a fail with a nested condition loses its nested
								     text in antrun, hence the separate conditions) -->
								<condition property="lib.wrong">
									<not>
										<and>
											<equals arg1="${lib.plain}" arg2="${lib.rest}" />
											<equals arg1="${lib.yfiles.count}" arg2="2" />
										</and>
									</not>
								</condition>
								<fail if="lib.wrong">

The lib/ of ${zip} must hold the jars of the plain bin zip and
exactly two more, ${backend.jar} and ${yfiles.jar}
from release/yfiles/target/lib. Of these two it holds ${lib.yfiles.count}; its other jars:

  ${lib.rest}

and those of the plain zip:

  ${lib.plain}

See zip.xml and pom.xml of ${project.artifactId}.
								</fail>
								<unzip src="${zip}" dest="${check.dir}/lib">
									<patternset>
										<include name="*/lib/${backend.jar}" />
										<include name="*/lib/${yfiles.jar}" />
									</patternset>
									<flattenmapper />
								</unzip>
								<macrodef name="check-obfuscated">
									<attribute name="jar" />
									<sequential>
										<fail message="The jar lib/@{jar} of ${zip} is not the obfuscated one of release/yfiles/target/lib: it differs from that one, or equals the input of the obfuscation in release/yfiles/target/in. A jar that has not been through yGuard must never be distributed; see zip.xml of ${project.artifactId}.">
											<condition>
												<not>
													<and>
														<filesmatch file1="${check.dir}/lib/@{jar}" file2="${obf.dir}/lib/@{jar}" />
														<not>
															<filesmatch file1="${check.dir}/lib/@{jar}" file2="${obf.dir}/in/@{jar}" />
														</not>
													</and>
												</not>
											</condition>
										</fail>
									</sequential>
								</macrodef>
								<check-obfuscated jar="${backend.jar}" />
								<check-obfuscated jar="${yfiles.jar}" />
								<!-- a binary with yFiles in it must carry the restrictions
								     that come with the library -->
								<resourcecount property="restrictions.count">
									<zipfileset src="${zip}" includes="*/LICENSE-YFILES.txt" />
								</resourcecount>
								<condition property="restrictions.missing">
									<not>
										<equals arg1="${restrictions.count}" arg2="1" />
									</not>
								</condition>
								<fail if="restrictions.missing">

${zip} has no LICENSE-YFILES.txt at its root.
A binary that contains the yFiles library must carry the restrictions that come
with it, in that file, which the zip takes from release/yfiles/include and the
installers show as part of their licence; see zip.xml of ${project.artifactId}.
								</fail>
								<sequential unless:true="${yfiles.smoke.skip}">
									<property name="smoke.dir" location="${check.dir}/smoke" />
									<property name="smoke.home" location="${smoke.dir}/${zip.basedir}" />
									<unzip src="${zip}" dest="${smoke.dir}" />
									<!-- the negative control: the plain launcher in the same tree -->
									<copy file="${project.basedir}/../../runnable/target/Imager.jar" tofile="${smoke.home}/bin/PlainImager.jar" />
									<macrodef name="imager">
										<attribute name="jar" />
										<attribute name="out" />
										<sequential>
											<mkdir dir="${smoke.dir}/@{out}" />
											<java jar="${smoke.home}/bin/@{jar}.jar" fork="true" jvm="${java.home}/bin/java" dir="${smoke.home}" failonerror="false" resultproperty="@{out}.result" outputproperty="@{out}.output">
												<jvmarg value="-Djava.awt.headless=true" />
												<arg value="-b" />
												<arg value="yfiles" />
												<arg value="-f" />
												<arg value="png" />
												<arg file="${smoke.grammar}" />
												<arg file="${smoke.dir}/@{out}" />
											</java>
											<resourcecount property="@{out}.pngs">
												<fileset dir="${smoke.dir}/@{out}" includes="**/*.png" />
											</resourcecount>
										</sequential>
									</macrodef>
									<imager jar="Imager" out="yfiles" />
									<imager jar="PlainImager" out="plain" />
									<condition property="smoke.failed">
										<or>
											<not>
												<equals arg1="${yfiles.result}" arg2="0" />
											</not>
											<equals arg1="${yfiles.pngs}" arg2="0" />
											<contains string="${yfiles.output}" substring="is not available" />
										</or>
									</condition>
									<fail if="smoke.failed">

The Imager of ${zip}, run headlessly on the unpacked zip
(${smoke.home}) with -b yfiles -f png on
${smoke.grammar}, did not render on the yFiles backend:
exit code ${yfiles.result}, ${yfiles.pngs} png files, and the output

${yfiles.output}

A warning that the backend is not available means that the obfuscated jars
are missing from the launcher's class path or do not load. Skip this check
with -Dyfiles.smoke.skip=true.
									</fail>
									<condition property="control.failed">
										<not>
											<contains string="${plain.output}" substring="is not available" />
										</not>
									</condition>
									<fail if="control.failed">

The plain Imager launcher, run on the unpacked yFiles zip
(${smoke.home}/bin/PlainImager.jar) with -b yfiles, did not warn that
the yFiles backend is not available; its output was

${plain.output}

The check of the yFiles launcher above recognises a fallback to JGraph by that
warning (see Imager.selectBackend), so its wording has probably changed: update
this pom to the new wording.
									</fail>
								</sequential>
							</target>
						</configuration>
					</execution>
				</executions>
			</plugin>
		</plugins>
	</build>
</project>
